    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "515137",
        "date_added": "2026-10-25 08:55:43",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static configuration recovery, 2026-10-25 UTC. Verified SHA-256; complete 412,608-byte ELF64 little-endian x86-64, stripped. The configuration decryptor at VA 0x40030f implements ChaCha20 with a 256-bit embedded key, 96-bit nonce and initial counter zero. The host accessor 0x40323f decrypts 15 bytes from VA 0x44804c and explicitly appends a terminator; the separate port accessor 0x4031e4 resets the stream to decrypt two bytes at VA 0x448000, then interprets them in network byte order. Recovered configured endpoint: hand.genddos.st:48101. Decoder passed the RFC 8439 block known-answer test and independently matched the cryptography library. At call site 0x402285 the resolved host and decoded port reach a connection helper that creates AF_INET/SOCK_STREAM and calls connect; this establishes a configured TCP control endpoint, not a claimed successful live connection. Public DNS during this review returned 94.154.43.68; the DNS timestamp is retained separately from the sample first-seen 2026-10-25 04:15:26. ThreatFox already lists the domain and IP:port as 1984347 and 1984346 under another reporter, so neither was resubmitted. MalwareBazaar labels this file Gafgyt while the existing ThreatFox records use Mirai; retain the source-label difference rather than treating the hostname or Spider-UA string alone as definitive family attribution. Common resolver IP strings 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8 are not C2 findings. No sample execution, C2 connection, exploit attempt, raw malware bytes or key material in this comment."
      }
    ],
